{"chunk_id": "81b0891af5d1", "text": "Surya, the sun-god and Karna\u2019s divine father, appears to Karna in a dream disguised as a Brahmana to warn him of a coming deception. Indra (Sakra), wishing to protect the Pandavas, plans to approach Karna in the same disguise and beg for Karna\u2019s natural armor and earrings\u2014divine protections born with him that make him nearly invincible. Surya urges Karna to refuse and instead offer other riches, explaining that giving them away will shorten his life and lead to his death in battle. Karna, however, refuses to abandon his vow of absolute generosity to Brahmanas. He declares that fame and honor are worth more than life itself, choosing lasting renown over survival. The episode highlights Karna\u2019s tragic nobility: his unwavering commitment to generosity and reputation ultimately drives him toward the fate his father fears.\nSurya warns Karna that Indra will beg for his divine armor and earrings, but Karna insists on giving them to preserve his vow and eternal fame.\nThemes: honor vs survival, fate and prophecy, divine parenthood, generosity and vows, fame and glory", "vector": [0.016996843740344048, -0.024602796882390976, -0.003536568721756339, -0.006806729361414909, -0.002930490067228675, 0.03247515857219696, -0.018635252490639687, -0.01323382742702961, -0.03074350580573082, -0.01578468643128872, 0.009097839705646038, 0.006333854980766773, 0.018688535317778587, 0.012561146169900894, -0.008851412683725357, -0.012348019517958164, 0.05051099509000778, -0.02219180203974247, 0.03250179812312126, -0.02600144036114216, -0.0075193713419139385, -0.002800616202875972, -0.01914142817258835, 0.03537900745868683, -0.019327914342284203, 0.00807882845401764, 0.020753199234604836, -0.035245805978775024, 0.026321129873394966, -0.039854664355516434, -0.0038429382257163525, -0.004878600127995014, -0.000835023180115968, 0.002344392007216811, -0.018462087959051132, 0.0038529285229742527, -0.003599840681999922, -0.019820770248770714, 